The $\pm$2\pp{} margin used in \S\ref{sec:equivalence} provides approximately 30\% headroom above the minimum equivalence margin ($\pm$1.52\pp{}). At the observed accuracy range of 85--88\%, a 2\pp{} gap corresponds to approximately 15 additional errors per 900 predictions, a threshold we consider practically meaningful for deployment decisions.


